<script src="/js/easy.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/menu.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/form.js?version=545"></script><script src="/js/inplace.js?version=545"></script><script>EC.version='545'</script></head>
<body><table class="page" id="page"><tr style="height:1px"><td><table class="header"><tr><td class="logocell"><a href="/" title="EasyChair home page"><img class="leftlogo" src="/images/logoEC_short.png"/></a></td><td class="rolecell">EasyChair Smart CFP</td><td style="width: 99%"></td><td class="helplink"><a class="toplinks" href="/docs/home" title="User guide">User guide</a></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr style="height:99%"><td class="menu_and_content"><div class="menu" id="menu0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="menu" style="position:static; visibility:visible"><tr><td class="top" id="menu1" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu1','/cfp',{&quot;a&quot;:null})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu1')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu1')" title="Main page">Home</td><td class="top" id="menu2" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu2','/cfp/choose',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu2')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu2')" title="Create a new CFP">New CFP</td><td class="top" id="menu3" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu3','/cfp/all',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu3')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu3')" title="Manage my CFPs">My CFPs</td><td class="top" id="menu4" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu4','/cfp/watchlist',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu4')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu4')" title="My CFP watchlist">Watchlist</td></tr></table></div><div class="search_row" id="cfp:search:row"><form action="/cfp/search" id="search-form"><input id="search-input" name="query" placeholder="Search" type="text"/></form></div><div class="summary"><div class="pagetitle">CFP</div></div><div class="content" id="content"><div class="subcontent"><div id="cfp" style="clear:right"><table class="title_table"><tr><td class="single"><div id="cfptitle">BMSB 2027: IEEE International Symposium on Broadband Multimedia Systems and Broadcasting 2027</div><div id="cfpvenue"></div><div id="cfpdateplace">Sydney, Australia, July 7-9, 2027</div></td></tr></table><table class="date_table"><tr><td>Conference web page</td><td><a href="https://www.bmsb2027.com/" target="_blank">https://www.bmsb2027.com/</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission link</td><td><a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=bmsb2027" target="_blank">https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=bmsb2027</a></td></tr><tr><td>Abstract registration deadline</td><td>January 15, 2027</td></tr><tr><td>Submission deadline</td><td>January 15, 2027</td></tr></table><div class="topics">Topics: <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=33284" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_bluelight bg_bluelight">multimedia transmission</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=183409" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_green bg_gray1">multimedia networking</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=1126500" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_black bg_wheat">multimedia signal processing</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=27375374" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_black bg_darksalmon">multimedia service and quality</span></a></div><p>BMSB 2027: IEEE International Symposium on Broadband Multimedia Systems and Broadcasting</p><p>7-9 July 2027, Sydney, Australia</p><p>Conference website: www.bmsb2027.com</p><p>Submission deadline: 15 January 2027</p><p>The IEEE International Symposium on Broadband Multimedia Systems and Broadcasting 2027 (BMSB 2027), the 22nd in the series, will be held on 7-9 July 2027 in Sydney, Australia. Sponsored by the IEEE Broadcast Technology Society, the symposium is the premier forum for the presentation and exchange of technical advances in the rapidly converging areas of multimedia broadcasting, telecommunications, consumer electronics, and networking technologies. BMSB 2027 is hosted by the AI Security &amp; Privacy (AISP) Lab at the Australian AI Institute (AAII), University of Technology Sydney.</p><h2>Submission Guidelines</h2><p>All papers must be original and not simultaneously submitted to another journal or conference. The following paper categories are welcome:</p><p>- Full papers (up to 6 pages) describing original, unpublished research results, systems, or field trials.</p><p>- Extended abstracts (up to 3 pages) describing work in progress, early results, or novel ideas.</p><p>Manuscripts must be submitted in PDF format using the IEEE conference template: https://www.ieee.org/conferences/publishing/templates</p><p>Please submit your paper via EasyChair: https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=bmsb2027</p><p>Important Dates</p><ul><li>Submission of extended abstract / full paper: <strong>15 January 2027</strong></li><li>Notification of acceptance: <strong>1 March 2027</strong></li><li>Submission of camera-ready papers: <strong>15 April 2027</strong></li></ul><h2>List of Topics</h2><p>The symposium seeks unpublished technical papers on topics including, but not limited to:</p><h3>1. Multimedia Transmission</h3><ul><li>Channel modelling and simulation</li><li>Channel coding, modulation, multiplexing</li><li>Advanced signal processing for transmission</li><li>MISO and MIMO processing</li><li>Channel estimation and equalization</li><li>Antenna technologies</li><li>Propagation and coverage</li><li>Terrestrial and satellite delivery</li><li>Mobile TV and advanced HD Radio</li><li>Field trials and test results</li><li>Next generation of broadcasting standards</li><li>UAV communication and route planning</li><li>AI-based communications</li><li>Technologies beyond 5G</li><li>Integrated sensing and multimedia distribution</li></ul><h3>2. Multimedia Networking</h3><ul><li>Multimedia for connected cars and IoT</li><li>Multimedia datacasting</li><li>Multimedia security</li><li>Quality evaluation and datasets</li><li>Audience measurement and behaviour study</li><li>Quality of experience</li><li>Future broadcasting services</li><li>Convergence of broadcast and broadband</li><li>Distributed or edge/fog-based multimedia services</li><li>Cloud-based multimedia services</li><li>6G NTN systems and networks</li></ul><h3>3. Multimedia Signal Processing</h3><ul><li>Multimedia coding: image, video, audio</li><li>Error resilience and concealment</li><li>3D, virtual reality, multi-view video</li><li>AI-based and generated multimedia coding</li><li>Scalable video coding and content adaptation</li><li>Retrieval and indexing</li><li>Synthetic imaging and rendering</li><li>Objective video and audio quality assessment</li></ul><h3>4. Multimedia Service and Quality</h3><ul><li>IPTV and streaming</li><li>Internet TV and OTT</li><li>FeMBMS, 5G NR MBS, MooD and SC-PTM</li><li>VoD, interactivity, datacasting</li><li>Multimedia NFV and SDN</li><li>Traffic and performance monitoring</li><li>Networking and QoS</li><li>Broadcast applications to smart cities</li><li>AI for multimedia networking intelligence</li><li>Broadcast core network</li><li>XR/VR/AR-based communications</li><li>RIS-assisted communications</li></ul><h3>5. Multimedia Security and Privacy</h3><ul><li>AI-generated content and deepfake detection</li><li>Misinformation and multimedia forensics</li><li>Digital watermarking</li><li>Privacy-preserving multimedia</li></ul><h2>Committees</h2><h3>General Chair</h3><ul><li>Bo Liu (Australia)</li></ul><h3>Technical Program Committee</h3><ul><li>Yiyan Wu (Canada)</li><li>Peng Yu (China)</li></ul><h3>Organizing Committee</h3><ul><li>Bo Liu (Executive Chair)</li><li>Kaiyue Feng (Publicity Chair)</li><li>Ryan Zhou (Registration Chair)</li><li>Shang Wang (Panel Chair)</li><li>Yang Sun (Industry Liaison Chair)</li><li>Peng Cheng (Sponsorship Chair)</li><li>Hellen Yu (IT Chair)</li><li>Ryan Zhou (Finance Chair)</li></ul><h3>International Steering Committee</h3><ul><li>Yiyan Wu (Canada)</li><li>Pablo Angueira (Spain)</li><li>David Gomez-Barquero (Spain)</li><li>Ralph Hogan (USA)</li><li>Shuji Hirakawa (Japan)</li><li>Samina Husain (Switzerland)</li><li>Gabriel-Miro Muntean (Ireland)</li><li>Maurizio Murroni (Italy)</li><li>Madeleine Noland (USA)</li><li>Sung-Ik Park (Korea)</li><li>Peter Siebert (Switzerland)</li><li>Jian Song (China)</li><li>Xianbin Wang (Canada)</li><li>Wenjun Zhang (China)</li></ul><h2>Venue</h2><p>The conference will be held at the University of Technology Sydney (UTS), 15 Broadway, Ultimo NSW 2007, Sydney, Australia.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>All questions about submissions should be emailed to <a href="mailto:info@bmsb2027.com">info@bmsb2027.com</a>. Sponsorship enquiries: <a href="mailto:sponsors@bmsb2027.com">sponsors@bmsb2027.com</a>.</p></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><td class="footer">Copyright © 2002 – 2026 EasyChair</td></tr></table></body></html>
